Coolstore splits an order total across line items for invoices; the parts must always sum to the original amount in cents. Write JUnit 5 tests for this method, including edge cases:

public static long[] split(long totalCents, int parts) {
    long base = totalCents / parts;
    long[] out = new long[parts];
    Arrays.fill(out, base);
    out[parts - 1] += totalCents - base * parts;
    return out;
}

This Coolstore inventory update loses stock changes under concurrent requests. Explain why and give a fix using JPA optimistic locking:

